# The server's image (Dockerfile.server) is built from the repository's root, as the one Cargo workspace's member: this
# file (BuildKit reads it in place of the root's .dockerignore) lets in only what cargo reads for it. Never build output,
# the proofs, the plans, the page or the tile's scripts; each crate's tests, which a release build never compiles, stay
# out too, so a change to one leaves the image as it was.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!aven/db/crates
aven/db/crates/*/tests
!aven/db/vendor/iroh
# theOS's crates are members of the workspace: cargo reads their manifests and finds their targets, and builds none
!theos/app/Cargo.toml
!theos/app/src
!theos/crates/*/Cargo.toml
!theos/crates/*/src
